<p>As of 25<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>June<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>2025<sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=SARS-CoV-2_Omicron_variant&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=SARS-CoV-2_Omicron_variant&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup>, the variants of interest as specified by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./World_Health_Organization" title="World Health Organization">World Health Organization</a> are JN.1, and the variants under monitoring are KP.3, KP.3.1.1, JN.1.18, LP.8.1, NB.1.8.1, XEC and XFG.<sup about="#mwt115" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Variants_of_SARS-CoV-2_current_variants_27-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Variants of SARS-CoV-2 current_variants"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Variants_of_SARS-CoV-2_current_variants-27"}}'><a href="./SARS-CoV-2_Omicron_variant#cite_note-Variants_of_SARS-CoV-2_current_variants-27" id="mwmg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwmw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwnA">[</span>27<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwnQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
